# TZ-232 — Angular Assembly DSL: Master Plan с встроенной защитой и полной дорожной картой

**Дата создания:** 2026-07-27 (обновлено 2026-07-27 после PO decisions)
**Автор:** senior-architect review
**Приоритет:** STRATEGIC (определяет архитектуру семейства Angular-проектов на годы вперёд)
**Связь:** SUCCESSOR для `DEVELOPMENT-PATTERNS.md §1-§10` и audit TZ-176/177/178 (миграция сигналов); ABSORBS TZ-179 (`any`-cleanup → ESLint rule)
**Скоу:** foundational design + полный migration checklist для текущего проекта. **Ядро стабильно для повторного использования**.

---

## 0. TL;DR для PO

**Цель Master Plan:** навести полный порядок в Angular-проекте, мигрировав ВСЕ существующие list-страницы и form-диалоги на единый DSL, разложив god-component на атомарные части, и **жёстко** заблокировав небезопасные паттерны на compile-time + runtime + lint-level.

**Что НЕ делаем:** никаких абстракций «на вырост». Ядро DSL — стабильно для повторного использования в будущих Angular-проектах этого семейства (через конфигурируемые entity), но **никакого** "универсального BlockRenderer DSL" по решению PO — декомпозиция делается на конкретные переиспользуемые Pieces.

**Объём внедрения (точно):**

| Тип | Количество | Суммарный объём |
|---|---|---|
| List-pages к миграции | 13 | 11 простых/средних + 2 средних + 1 dashboard-композиция |
| Form-dialogs к миграции | 10 | 4 простых + 4 средних (FormArray) + 2 сложных |
| Builder atomic parts | 9 | 6 компонентов + 2 сервиса + 1 facade |
| Sub-TZ (work breakdown) | 14 | TZ-232.A через TZ-232.N |

**Реалистичный объём работы:** **~140–180 часов** (5-7 sessions). Sequential dependency → фактически 3-4 calendar weeks при dedicated session.

---

## 1. Встроенная защита (Po-level обязательная фича)

**Принцип:** Защита от небезопасного кода встраивается В ЯДРО DSL, а не добавляется post-hoc. Любая попытка обойти должна ловиться **хотя бы одной** из трёх защитных линий (lint, compile-time, runtime).

### 1.1 Защита от двойного сабмита (double-click → duplicates)

**Проблема:** В 8 form-dialog есть `submitting = signal(false)` + `[disabled]="form.invalid || submitting()"`. **Но:**
- Только 5 из 8 имеют guard `if (this.submitting()) return;` в начале `onSubmit()` (отсутствует в organizations, products, modules, contracts).
- custom submit handlers (не через форму) могут проскочить disabled toggle, если нажатие происходит между двумя CD cycles (< 200ms rapid clicks).
- **На бэкенде нет idempotency** — повторный POST создаст дубль.

**Решение — 3 уровня:**

#### Уровень 1 + 2 — `SubmitGuard` и HTTP-interceptor как единая коррелированная система (FIX C1 из review)

**Файлы:**
- `frontend/src/app/shared/dsl/submit-guard.ts` — singleton state holder, single source of UUIDs
- `frontend/src/app/core/idempotency.interceptor.ts` — HTTP-layer integration, READS ключ от SubmitGuard
- `frontend/src/app/core/idempotency-cache.ts` — Level 3 client cache

**КРИТИЧНО:** обе защиты читают/пишут **ОДИН Map**. НЕ генерируют UUID независимо. Это устраняет key-scope mismatch (CRITICAL issue из review): если у нас 2 независимых источника UUID, backend не может коррелировать replays.

```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class SubmitGuard {
  /**
   * SINGLE-SOURCE-OF-TRUTH for in-flight submit operations.
   * Holds correlation map: (URL+method+formKey) ↔ active Idempotency-Key (UUID).
   *
   * All three protection layers read/write THIS map:
   *   - Level 1 (`guard()`): rejects if entry exists; creates entry on accept.
   *   - Level 2 (HTTP interceptor): reads `getActiveKey()` for current URL+method.
   *     Frontend does NOT generate UUID independently.
   *   - Level 3 (client cache): stores completed results keyed by same composite key.
   *
   * Lifecycle:
   *   - guard() called → register entry with FRESH UUID
   *   - HTTP interceptor reads same UUID via getActiveKey() → headers propagate
   *   - debounce 300ms passes → fetcher fires → result stored in completedCache (5min TTL)
   *   - in-flight entry removed in finally{} regardless of fetcher outcome
   *
   * Re-entry (rapid double-click) → guard() sees active entry → returns 429 SilentResult
   * BEFORE any HTTP request fires. Idempotency-Key header NEVER reaches backend twice.
   */
  private readonly inFlight = new Map<string, string>(); // composite → UUID
  private readonly completedCache = new Map<string, {
    result: SilentResult<unknown>;
    expiresAt: number;
  }>(); // composite → { result, ttl }

  constructor() {
    // ── Background cache eviction (FIX REG-2 from review) ──
    // completedCache relies on passive TTL expiration; without this loop the Map
    // grows monotonically over app lifetime. In long-running sessions (admin tools,
    // kiosks) this becomes a memory leak. Sweep every 60s.
    setInterval(() => {
      const now = Date.now();
      for (const [k, v] of this.completedCache) {
        if (v.expiresAt <= now) this.completedCache.delete(k);
      }
    }, 60_000);
  }

  async guard<T>(opts: {
    formKey: string;        // e.g. "create:Order:formInstanceId"
    url: string;
    method: 'POST' | 'PATCH' | 'DELETE';
    debounceMs?: number;    // default 300ms
    fetcher: () => Observable<SilentResult<T>>;
  }): Promise<SilentResult<T>> {
    const composite = `${opts.method}|${opts.url}|${opts.formKey}`;

    // ── Level 3: completed cache hit → return previous result ──
    const cached = this.completedCache.get(composite);
    if (cached && cached.expiresAt > Date.now()) {
      return cached.result as SilentResult<T>;
    }

    // ── Level 1: re-entry guard → reject if in-flight ──
    if (this.inFlight.has(composite)) {
      return {
        ok: false,
        error: new HttpErrorResponse({
          status: 429,
          statusText: 'Already in flight',
          error: { message: 'Подождите завершения предыдущей операции' },
        }),
      };
    }

    // Generate UUID — bind to interceptor ONLY AFTER debounce (FIX REG-1 from review).
    // Registering BEFORE debounce creates a 300ms cross-component contamination
    // window: any HTTP POST/PATCH/DELETE from OTHER components during debounce
    // would pick up this form's UUID via interceptor's getActiveKey(url, method)
    // and inherit a wrong Idempotency-Key → cross-component contamination.
    //
    // Trade-off: brief unprotected moment (sub-ms) between debounce completion
    // and firstValueFrom() firing. Acceptable because debounce itself already
    // filters rapid-double-click on the same form (~300ms >> typical human
    // double-click latency of ~150ms).
    const key = crypto.randomUUID();

    try {
      // Debounce: rapid double-clicks within window collapse to single fire.
      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, opts.debounceMs ?? 300));

      // Register AFTER debounce, immediately before HTTP fires. Window
      // between this line and fetcher() invocation is sub-ms in V8(no async
      // boundary — Promise resolution runs synchronously in microtask), so
      // double-click protection is effectively atomic.
      this.inFlight.set(composite, key);

      // The fetcher flows through idempotencyInterceptor which reads
      // getActiveKey(url, method) → returns the SAME UUID we just registered.
      const result = await firstValueFrom(opts.fetcher());

      // ── Level 3: graded cache policy (FIX review regression) ──
      //   ok:true → cache 5 min (lost ACK + rapid-double-submit защита).
      //   5xx   → cache 60 s (retry storm на упавшем сервере, юзер подождёт >60s).
      //   4xx   → НЕ кешируется (юзер ОБЯЗАН исправить форму и повторить СРАЗУ;
      //                    иначе stale cached error после исправления).
      if (result.ok) {
        this.completedCache.set(composite, {
          result,
          expiresAt: Date.now() + 5 * 60 * 1000,
        });
      } else if (result.error.status >= 500) {
        this.completedCache.set(composite, {
          result,
          expiresAt: Date.now() + 60 * 1000,
        });
      }
      // else: 4xx → no cache → next submit reaches server.
      return result;
    } finally {
      this.inFlight.delete(composite);
    }
  }

  /**
   * Read-only access for the HTTP interceptor.
   * Returns the active Idempotency-Key for a given (URL+method) if there's an
   * in-flight submission, OR null if no submit is active.
   *
   * IMPORTANT: returns whichever formKey is currently active for this URL.
   * Multiple instanced forms targeting same endpoint race against each other
   * — for current architecture (one active dialog at a time) this is safe.
   */
  getActiveKey(url: string, method: string): string | null {
    const prefix = `${method}|${url}|`;
    for (const [composite, key] of this.inFlight) {
      if (composite.startsWith(prefix)) return key;
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

#### Уровень 2: Idempotency-header в HTTP-interceptor (READ-ONLY)

```typescript
/**
 * Reads active UUID from SubmitGuard (Level 1) and attaches as header.
 * Does NOT generate UUID independently — that would break key correlation.
 *
 * If no submission is currently in-flight for this URL+method, generates
 * a fresh UUID anyway (for backend protection for service-level mutations
 * that bypass SubmitGuard — e.g. login, refresh, raw service.post calls
 * outside <pi-entity-form>).
 */
export const idempotencyInterceptor: HttpInterceptorFn = (req, next) => {
  const guard = inject(SubmitGuard);
  if (!/^(POST|PATCH|DELETE)$/.test(req.method)) return next(req);
  if (req.headers.has('Idempotency-Key')) return next(req);

  // Read from SubmitGuard.ifthere's an active submit for this URL.
  // Otherwise generate fresh (e.g. service-level mutations outside dialogs).
  const key = guard.getActiveKey(req.url, req.method) ?? crypto.randomUUID();
  return next(req.clone({ setHeaders: { 'Idempotency-Key': key } }));
};
```

#### Уровень 3: Client-side cache (auto-cleanup via TTL)

`completedCache` в SubmitGuard auto-expires entries через 5 min. Это решает:
- "Lost ACK" — POST прошёл, ответ не дошёл, повторный submit → cache hit → возвращаем старый результат. No double-create.
- Network retry storm — пользователь жмёт submit несколько раз в течение 5 min после первого успеха → cache returns prior result. No duplicate.

**TTL trade-off:** 5 min — pragmatic для UX форм. Backend может override через свой TTL в idempotency-record table.

### 1.2 Блокировка raw `this.http.*` (compile + lint)

**ESLint rules** (TZ-232.I):

```typescript
// frontend/eslint/rules/no-raw-http-in-components.ts
// Apply to *.component.ts files (not services, not core/silent-http.ts).
// BAN: any 'this.http.<verb>(...)' usage where 'this' resolves to Component class.
// ALLOW: *.service.ts and *.interceptor.ts (where explicit HTTP use is vetted).
//
// AST pattern:
//   CallExpression[callee.object.property.name='http']
//                 [callee.property.name=/^(post|get|put|patch|delete)$/]
//                 AND scope is ClassDeclaration extending Component decorator

// Also: BAN direct import of HttpClient from @angular/common/http in component files:
no-restricted-imports({
  paths: [{
    name: '@angular/common/http',
    importNames: ['HttpClient'],
    message: 'HttpClient запрещён в компонентах. Используйте DSL Repository через defineEntity().'
  }],
  patterns: ['*.component.ts']
})
// Note: HttpParams, HttpErrorResponse, httpResource ARE allowed in components (used by lookup-tables)
```

### 1.3 Type-safety через `defineEntity<T, P>`

**Решение (из §2 architecture):**

```typescript
// Coerced compile-time guards через TypeScript's type narrowing:
export function defineEntity<T extends { _id?: string }, P>(schema: EntitySchema<T, P>) {
  // Returns ONLY a typed entity token — service methods are accessible
  // only via `entity.inject()` inside a Component or Service injection context.
  // Cannot bypass by importing underlying HttpClient directly because:
  //  - HttpClient import is ESLint-banned in *.component.ts (см. §1.2)
  //  - defineEntity() requires schema.endpoint to be `string` literal
  //  - methods are typed for T, P → PATCH/POST body must match T's shape
  //  - missing _id update → compile error
}
```

**Compile-time errors (cannot be bypassed):**

| Попытка | Реакция |
|---|---|
| `defineEntity({})` (без endpoint) | TS error: `{ endpoint: string }` required |
| `defineEntity({ endpoint: 42 })` | TS error: `string` expected |
| `entity.create({ wrongType: 'x' } as any)` | TS error: `Partial<T>` cannot include `wrongType` if not in T |
| `<pi-entity-list [endpoint]="">` (literal typo) | When `endpoint: '/users'` declared and used elsewhere — RT error (request 404) AND audit-test catches in spec |
| `this.http.post(...)` in `*.component.ts` | ESLint error: `no-raw-http-in-components` |
| `service.update(id, payload)` where `id` is a `number` | TS error (mongo ObjectId is string-typed) |

### 1.4 Other safety mechanisms built into DSL

| Risky pattern | DSL protection |
|---|---|
| `OnInit` в page-component (legacy) | ESLint rule `no-implements-oninit-in-pages` (warning) + guidance → use `effect()` or `ngOnInit` исключительно в инфраструктурных сервисах |
| `any` type | ESLint rule `no-explicit-any` (error в dsl-config files; warning в pages). ANT-targets config from `defineEntity()` itself. |
| Missing `submitting` guard в custom submit | Type-level: `entity.create()` returns Promise → if called twice while pending, second-awaiter gets same Promise (deduplicated by Guard) |
| Множественные `<form>` в одном component | ESLint rule: at most one `<form>` without explicit `name` attribute |
| Memory leak от raw `.subscribe()` outside dsl-service | ESLint rule `no-restricted-syntax` catches `this.http.X.subscribe(...)` pattern |
| Lookup-table leak (TZ-232.A fixed) | Wizard: `defineLookup` returns `Signal<Record<id,T>>` + auto-cleanup через `DestroyRef.onDestroy(() => fetcher.unsubscribe())` |

